            <ArticleTitle>Obesity corrupts myelopoiesis.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>735-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1016/j.cmet.2014.04.010</ELocationID>
            <ELocationID EIdType="pii" ValidYN="Y">S1550-4131(14)00174-0</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Ongoing monocyte infiltration and subsequent macrophage seeding of adipose tissue is thought to be a key feature of obesity pathophysiology. Nagareddy et al. (2014) show that adipose cells locally activate IL-1β in macrophages in part through the alarmin S100A8/A9, which stimulates bone marrow myelopoiesis to perpetuate nonresolving inflammation.</AbstractText>
